## Rules for legacy code

- New and modified code meets the standard; legacy debt is fixed only when a phase explicitly scopes it.
- Moving code = move + update every caller + delete the old file in the same phase; no shims (see `no-wrapper-rule.md` if generated).
- Do not create empty future layers or duplicate canonical implementations.
- Each phase leaves a runnable, checkable system; reviewers block on regressions, not unrelated debt.

